  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1025 PM CDT Sat May 16 2026\n\nHighs near and into the low-90s will continue for one more day on \nTuesday ahead of our next chance for rain relief. By Tuesday, a \nlarge upper-level trough will develop over the Plains and increasing \nsoutherly flow ahead of it will bring in higher moisture values with \nPWATs increasing to over 1.5 inches. This brings a high chance for \nrain late Tuesday through Wednesday before the front pushes through \neither late Wednesday or Thursday. Hopefully this is decent rain \nwhich we do really need. Latest model guidance shows about a 40-50% \nchance of getting above an inch by Thursday. It is several days out \nstill to talk about any potential for hazardous weather, but it \nis worth noting that the setup doesn't look favorable right now \nwith better shear to the north and displaced from the higher \ninstability to the south. \n\nBehind the front, temperatures will cool to more seasonable values \nwith highs in the upper-70s to low-80s Thursday into next weekend. \nLow confidence in the overall pattern late next week, but it looks \nto remain unsettled enough to keep low to medium rain chances in the \nforecast beyond Thursday.",
